edge_count: 2
complexity: time=O(1) | space=O(n)
complexity_note: Give the time of one call; n is the number of calls.
why_time: push makes one node, pop reads one link, and top and size read one entry.
why_space: Each push makes one node, and each version keeps a head and a size.
hint: push: `self.heads.append(Node(x, self.heads[v]))` and `self.sizes.append(self.sizes[v] + 1)`, then return `len(self.heads) - 1`.
hint: pop: append `self.heads[v].next` and `self.sizes[v] - 1` in the same way.
hint: top: return −1 if `self.heads[v]` is None, and its val otherwise.
right: Inserting at the front never changes the nodes after it, so every version can share the nodes of the version it came from, and a new version costs O(1) instead of a copy.
wrong: Store each version as a head node and a size. push makes a new node in front of version v's head; pop uses the node after version v's head; both append the new head and size, and return the new index.

=== task: code hard
title: Group by Remainder
